WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.850
Each output is evidence for something
specific, against NIST's control catalog.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.113
A policy that lets the reader's
group read announcements and

3
00:00:08.113 --> 00:00:11.637
nothing else supports monitoring
an external service provider.

4
00:00:11.637 --> 00:00:15.556
A run folder showing every chain's
latest announcement was read,

5
00:00:15.556 --> 00:00:20.437
in the right realm, supports that and
receiving security alerts and advisories.

6
00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:25.330
Maintenance that names the agency's
resources supports contingency planning,

7
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:28.888
because Chapter 6 asks the
system owner to review the plan.

8
00:00:28.888 --> 00:00:33.449
And a rescheduled window that stays one
notice supports continuous monitoring.

9
00:00:33.449 --> 00:00:37.375
The indicators are FedRAMP's;
the mapping is the program's.

10
00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:39.600
The assessor decides the controls.
